{:fh/id  "FH-CTRL-002"
 :fh/law "Two occurrences of one view given the SAME :control address share ONE record deliberately — an edit at either occurrence is read by both, no diagnostic fires, and the sharing is a consequence of the caller supplying the address rather than an accident of render position."

 :kind :my.ui/buffered-field

 ;; ONE address, passed to BOTH occurrences, ON PURPOSE. This is how two
 ;; views onto one draft are spelled: the address is the caller's
 ;; statement about WHICH state this is, so passing it twice is a claim
 ;; that these two sites edit the same thing. A derived anchor could not
 ;; express it at all — two occurrences would necessarily differ.
 :control [:invoice 42 :amount]

 ;; Both occurrences are given the same external baseline, as two views
 ;; onto one value would be.
 :value "100.00"

 ;; The edit is made at occurrence A. Occurrence B is a passive reader
 ;; of the same record and does nothing.
 :typed "99."

 ;; Both occurrences display the draft: one record, two readers.
 :displayed-after-edit ["99." "99."]

 ;; Exactly ONE record exists — sharing is one record read twice, not two
 ;; records kept in step.
 :record-keys-after-edit [[:my.ui/buffered-field [:invoice 42 :amount]]]

 ;; Sharing is a FEATURE. Nothing about a second occurrence at the same
 ;; address is diagnosed: the render of both occurrences raises nothing.
 :diagnosed? false}
